{title: I Need Thee Every Hour}
{artist: Annie Hawks & Robert Lowry}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[G]I need thee every [C]hour, most [G]gracious [D]Lord;
[G]no tender voice like [C]thine can [G]peace [D]af[G]ford.

Chorus
I [G]need thee, O I [C]need thee — [G]every hour I [D]need thee!
O [G]bless me [C]now, my [G]Savior: [D]I come to [G]thee!

Verse 2
[G]I need Thee ev'ry hour, Stay Thou near by; Temptations [C]lose their pow'r When [G]Thou art nigh. [D]I need
[G]Thee, O I need Thee; Ev'ry hour I need Thee; [C]O bless me now, my [G]Savior, I come [D]to Thee!

Verse 3
[G]I need Thee ev'ry hour, In joy or pain; Come [C]quickly and abide, Or [G]life is vain. [D]I need
[G]Thee, O I need Thee; Ev'ry hour I need Thee; [C]O bless me now, my [G]Savior, I come [D]to Thee!

Verse 4
[G]I need Thee ev'ry hour, Teach me Thy will; And [C]Thy rich promises In [G]me fulfill. I [D]need Thee,
[G]O I need Thee; Ev'ry hour I need Thee; O [C]bless me now, my [G]Savior, I come [D]to Thee!

Verse 5
[G]I need Thee ev'ry hour, Most Holy One; O make [C]me Thine indeed, Thou [G]blessed Son! I [D]need Thee,
[G]O I need Thee; Ev'ry hour I need Thee; O [C]bless me now, my [G]Savior, I come [D]to Thee!
